To create a web page that displays an image with a caption underneath it using HTML and CSS, follow these steps:

1. **Create the HTML structure**: The basic structure of your webpage will include a `div` container (`#img-container`) where the image and caption will be placed.

2. **Add the image**: Place an `<img>` tag inside the `#img-container`, linking it to the desired URL (e.g., "image.jpg").

3. **Add the caption**: Include a `<p>` tag within the same `#img-container` to display the caption.

4. **Style the elements**: Apply styles using CSS to center the image, ensure the image scales appropriately, and adjust the spacing for better readability.

Here is how you can implement all these steps in your HTML file:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Image with Caption</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            line-height: 1.6;
            color: #333;
            background-color: #f4f4f9;
        }

        #img-container {
            text-align: center;
            padding-top: 50px; /* Add some space between the image and the caption */
        }

        #img-container img {
            width: 100%; /* Make sure the image covers its parent container */
            height: auto; /* Maintain aspect ratio of the image */
        }

        #img-container p {
            margin: 0;
            font-size: 14px;
            color: #777;
            opacity: 0.8; /* Adjust opacity as needed */
            transition: opacity 0.3s ease-in-out;
        }

        #img-container:hover p {
            opacity: 1;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

<div id="img-container">
    <a href="http://www.example.com"><img src="image.jpg" alt="Image"></a>
    <p>Caption goes here</p>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### Explanation of Styles:
- **CSS Background Color**: Sets a light gray background color for the body to enhance readability.
- **Text Alignment**: Centers the content both horizontally and vertically within the `#img-container`.
- **Image Styling**:
  - `width: 100%`: Ensures the image takes up the full width of its containing div while maintaining its original aspect ratio.
  - `height: auto`: Keeps the image's height proportional to its width without distorting its shape.
- **Caption Styling**:
  - The caption is styled to appear at the bottom of the image container when hovered over or clicked.
  - It starts with normal transparency but changes to fully visible on hover, adding interactivity through a simple CSS transition effect.

This setup ensures that your image is displayed prominently with a clear caption below it, enhancing user engagement and navigation experience.

