Implementing a text editor with multiple list support in Angular involves several steps, including setting up the HTML structure, using Angular Material for UI components, and integrating an external library or service for editing functionality.

### Step 1: Setup Your Project

First, make sure you have Angular installed on your system. If not, install it via npm:

```bash
npm install -g @angular/cli
```

Then, create a new Angular project:

```bash
ng new my-text-editor-app
cd my-text-editor-app
```

Install `ngx-material-components` (a collection of material components):

```bash
npm install ngx-material-components --save
```

Add `@angular/cdk` if you need CDK features like drag-and-drop:

```bash
npm install @angular/cdk --save
```

Finally, add `ngx-file-saver` for saving files:

```bash
npm install ngx-file-saver --save
```

### Step 2: Create the Text Editor Component

Create a component that will contain both the text editor and the multi-lists:

```bash
ng generate component text-editor
```

Open the newly generated file (`text-editor.component.ts`) and import necessary modules:

```typescript
import { Component } from '@angular/core';
import { MatListModule } from '@angular/material/list';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-text-editor',
  templateUrl: './text-editor.component.html',
  styleUrls: ['./text-editor.component.css']
})
export class TextEditorComponent {
  // Add any data members here if needed
}
```

### Step 3: Implement Multi-Lists

For simplicity, let's assume we want two lists: one for items in the text editor, and another for comments. We'll use `MatList` and `MatDivider`.

#### Template (text-editor.component.html)

```html
<div>
  <textarea [(ngModel)]="editorContent"></textarea>

  <!-- List for editing -->
  <mat-list [formControl]="editForm">
    <mat-list-item *ngFor="let item of items; let i = index" role="presentation">
      {{ item }}
      <button mat-icon-button aria-label="Edit" (click)="toggleEditMode(i)">
        <mat-icon>create</mat-icon>
      </button>
    </mat-list-item>
  </mat-list>

  <!-- Comment list -->
  <div>
    <h5>Comments:</h5>
    <mat-list #commentsList>
      <mat-list-item *ngFor="let comment of comments">{{ comment }}</mat-list-item>
      <button mat-raised-button color="primary" (click)="addComment()">
        Add Comment
      </button>
    </mat-list>
  </div>
</div>
```

